  "question": {
    "text": "Two particles of the same mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> are moving in circular orbits because of force,&nbsp;given by <math><mi>F</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The first particle is at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, and the second, at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. The best estimate for the ratio of kinetic energies of the first and the second particle is closest to",
